invariant: INV-17
file: ghash_hw.c
catches: ghash_equiv_test
reason: the AES=hw GHASH data loop wipes its state only up to the powers
  of the hash subkey, so H^1 to H^8 stay in the dead frame after every
  call, and a later caller's uninitialized stack reads them. Each is a
  function of the key, and H^1 is the subkey itself. No output changes,
  so no vector notices. bin/ghash_equiv_test copies the stack below one
  call over three passes and requires no power of H in the copy.

--- old
    ct_wipe(&s, offsetof(ghash_state, powers) + powers * sizeof s.powers[0]);
--- new
    ct_wipe(&s, offsetof(ghash_state, powers));
